# Python object slicing

Each case supplies the same Auto source to the ordinary AV run and the A2PY run-py check. The independent Python reference and required interpreter setup live in the python-1127 fixture directory.

## Case: numpy-torch
id: "py.slicing.1127.numpy-torch"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1127"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.as"
syntax: "auto-script"

```auto
use.py builtins: range
use.py numpy: array
use.py torch: arange

fn main() int {
    var n = array(range(6))
    var axis_source = 0
    for axis_source < 2 {
        var row = n
        if axis_source == 1 {
            row = arange(6)
        }
        print(row[0:3:2].tolist().to(str))
        print(row[:3].tolist().to(str))
        print(row[2:].tolist().to(str))
        print(row[:].tolist().to(str))
        print(row[1:4:].tolist().to(str))
        print(row[::2].tolist().to(str))
        print(row[-3:].tolist().to(str))
        if axis_source == 0 {
            print(row[::-1].tolist().to(str))
            print(row[4:0:-2].tolist().to(str))
            print(row[::-1][0].to(int))
        }
        axis_source = axis_source + 1
    }

    return 0
}
```

